Rewrite this so it builds the result without repeated string concatenation in a loop.
Behaviour, including the trailing-separator handling, must be identical. Submit the whole rewritten
function as join_words.

def join_words(words, sep):
    out = ""
    for w in words:
        out = out + w + sep
    if out:
        out = out[:-len(sep)]
    return out

